{"type":"base","_stats":{"modifiedTime":1757511377000,"systemId":"never-stop-blowing-up","lastModifiedBy":"foundryUser","systemVersion":"1.0.0","createdTime":1757447867325,"coreVersion":"12.343"},"flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"name":"Never Stop Blowing Up - Rules","img":"icons/svg/book.svg","_id":"never-stop-blowing-up-rules","folder":null,"sort":0,"system":{},"pages":[{"image":{},"sort":0,"type":"text","src":null,"text":{"content":"\u003ch1\u003eNever Stop Blowing Up - Game Rules\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWelcome to Never Stop Blowing Up, the explosive tabletop RPG where action never stops!\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003eQuick Access\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDigital Rulebook PDF:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href=\"assets/Never_Stop_Blowing_Up_Rules.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"\u003e Open Full Rules PDF\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eRight-click the link above and select \"Open in New Tab\" or \"Save Link As\" to download the complete rulebook.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch1\u003eHow to Play\u003c/h1\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003eStarting the Game\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eBuild your character choosing:\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAn Action Hero Name\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eA Catchphrase\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThree Abilities\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003eCharacter Skills\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eYou have 9 key skills:\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Stunts:\u003c/strong\u003e Parkour, climbing, acrobatics, speed\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Brawl:\u003c/strong\u003e Hand-to-hand combat, physical confrontation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Tough:\u003c/strong\u003e Endurance, resistance, survival, willpower\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Tech:\u003c/strong\u003e Computer systems, digital security, technology\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Weapons:\u003c/strong\u003e Firearms, melee weapons, ranged combat\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Drive:\u003c/strong\u003e Vehicle operation, chases, piloting\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Sneak:\u003c/strong\u003e Stealth, infiltration, subterfuge\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Wits:\u003c/strong\u003e Investigation, knowledge, problem-solving\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Hot:\u003c/strong\u003e Social interaction, charm, persuasion, charisma\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eEach skill starts at a d4.\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003eBlowing Up\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery time an action hero gets the highest value on their die, it \u003cstrong\u003e\"blows up\"\u003c/strong\u003e and that skill moves up to the next die type.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoll that new die and add the results to the current check.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf that new roll is also the highest value, the skill continues to \u003cstrong\u003eblow up.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRepeat this process until you reach a d20.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003eExample:\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou roll a d6 for a Weapons check\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou roll a 6  The 6 counts, roll again!\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou roll another 6  Now you have 12, roll again!\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou roll a 3  Final result is 15 (6+6+3)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis explosive mechanic creates unpredictable, escalating action that defines the \"Never Stop Blowing Up\" experience!\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003ePrepared Actions\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen an Action Hero has time to prepare for a skill check and is not under stress, they can use a \u003cstrong\u003eprepared action\u003c/strong\u003e. Instead of rolling a die, they take half the die value for that stat.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003eTurbo Tokens\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen an Action Hero fails a check they get a \u003cstrong\u003eTurbo Token\u003c/strong\u003e, which can be spent one-to-one to increase the value of a die roll.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf a die roll is increased to its highest value, it triggers a blow up as if the highest value had been rolled. Spent \u003cstrong\u003eTurbo Tokens\u003c/strong\u003e are placed on a player-specific tray in front of the board.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf both characters are in the same scene, players can spend \u003cstrong\u003eTurbo Tokens\u003c/strong\u003e for friends, but at 2x cost.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003eExample:\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou have 3 \u003cstrong\u003eTurbo Tokens\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou roll a d6 for a Weapons check\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou roll a 5  You add 1 \u003cstrong\u003eTurbo Token\u003c/strong\u003e to the roll, making it a 6 and trigger it to \u003cstrong\u003eBlow Up\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou now roll a d8  Getting a 6. You add your remaining 2 \u003cstrong\u003eTurbo Tokens\u003c/strong\u003e to the roll, blowing it up again!\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou now roll a d10, getting a 3  Final result is 17 (6+8+3).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003eInjury\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere are three injury levels:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSuperficial\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSevere\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAdrenalized\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen an Action Hero fails a \u003cstrong\u003eTough Check\u003c/strong\u003e by 5 or more, they take an \u003cstrong\u003eInjury Level\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt \u003cstrong\u003eSevere Injury\u003c/strong\u003e, players must spend double the amount of \u003cstrong\u003eTurbo Tokens\u003c/strong\u003e (i.e., 2 Turbo Tokens to Blow Up a 5 on a d6).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt the \u003cstrong\u003eAdrenalized\u003c/strong\u003e injury level, the injured character receives 10 \u003cstrong\u003eTurbo Tokens\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen an Adrenalized character fails a \u003cstrong\u003eTough Check\u003c/strong\u003e, they become either \u003cstrong\u003eIncapacitated\u003c/strong\u003e or \u003cstrong\u003eDead\u003c/strong\u003e, depending on the attacker\u0027s intention.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003eQuick Play Tips\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStart Small:\u003c/strong\u003e Begin with d4 or d6 dice and work your way up\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEmbrace Explosions:\u003c/strong\u003e When dice explode, lean into the chaos and escalation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUse Turbo Tokens Wisely:\u003c/strong\u003e Save them for crucial moments or dramatic reveals\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWork as a Team:\u003c/strong\u003e Group abilities are powerful when coordinated\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eKeep it Moving:\u003c/strong\u003e The game thrives on momentum and escalating action\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003eDifficulty Classes\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEasy:\u003c/strong\u003e DC 5-8\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eModerate:\u003c/strong\u003e DC 9-12\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHard:\u003c/strong\u003e DC 13-16\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVery Hard:\u003c/strong\u003e DC 17-20\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNearly Impossible:\u003c/strong\u003e DC 21+\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","format":1},"ownership":{"default":0},"name":"Game Rules","flags":{},"_id":"game-rules","title":{"level":1,"show":true},"video":{}},{"image":{},"sort":100,"type":"text","src":null,"text":{"content":"\u003ch1\u003eAbilities\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt the end of each session, players may use remaining \u003cstrong\u003eTurbo Tokens\u003c/strong\u003e to purchase extra abilities. Individual abilities cost 2 Turbo Tokens.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e By the Book:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Hot Check by 3 when interacting with authority figures\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Burglar:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Sneak Check by 3 when entering a protected location\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Connected:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Hot Check by 3 when searching for a helpful ally\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Demolitions:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Tech Check by 3 when explosives are involved\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Duelist:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Weapons Check by 3 against someone wielding the same weapon\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Escape Artist:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Sneak Check by 3 when escaping restraints or imprisonment\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Flashy:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Hot Check by 5 if it\u0027s the first roll after you\u0027ve Blown Up\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Grit:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Tough Check by 3 when resisting a Brawl Check\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Hacker:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Tech Check by 3 when breaking into a computer database\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Hotwire:\u003c/strong\u003e When interacting with vehicles, use Drive instead of Tech\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Inspiring:\u003c/strong\u003e Each time you succeed at a check, an ally of your choice receives 1 Turbo Token\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Interrogator:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Wits Check by 3 to draw information out of an opponent\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Leap of Faith:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Stunts Check by 3 when making a jump that could injure you\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Loyal:\u003c/strong\u003e Your Turbo Tokens give friends +1 at a one-to-one rate\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Lucky:\u003c/strong\u003e Spend 2 Turbo Tokens to reroll any check \u003cem\u003e(Once Per Episode)\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Martial Artist:\u003c/strong\u003e Spend a Turbo Token to force an enemy to resist your Brawl with Wits instead of Tough\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Menacing:\u003c/strong\u003e Use Brawl instead of Hot when intimidating an NPC\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Nerves of Steel:\u003c/strong\u003e Spend a Turbo Token to treat a snap decision as a Prepared Action\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Poker Face:\u003c/strong\u003e When attempting to conceal the truth, use Tough instead of Hot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Prepared:\u003c/strong\u003e Spend 2 Turbo Tokens to just happen to have one commonplace item with you \u003cem\u003e(GM\u0027s Discretion)\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Protector:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a check by 3 when defending your friends\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Quick Healing:\u003c/strong\u003e Recover one injury level at the end of an encounter\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Relentless:\u003c/strong\u003e Gain 2 Turbo Tokens when you fail a check\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Resilient:\u003c/strong\u003e Turbo Tokens are worth double when used to boost against an attack that targets you\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Skilled:\u003c/strong\u003e Increase your die type for one skill by 1 for the purposes of halving\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Smokin\u0027:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Hot Check by 3 when making a first impression\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Stealthy:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Sneak Check by 3 when trying to avoid being seen\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Trained:\u003c/strong\u003e -1 to DCs for a Stat of your choice\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Studied:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003cem\u003e(Replaces Trained)\u003c/em\u003e -3 to DCs for Stat of your choice\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Mastery:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003cem\u003e(Replaces Studied)\u003c/em\u003e -5 to DCs for a Stat of your choice\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Transporter:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Drive Check by 3 to avoid pursuers\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Trouble Maker:\u003c/strong\u003e Spend a Turbo Token to locate and receive help from a criminal network \u003cem\u003e(GM\u0027s Discretion)\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Wealthy:\u003c/strong\u003e Spend a Turbo Token to ease a bad situation with cash\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Wild Card:\u003c/strong\u003e You are a Wild Card\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","format":1},"ownership":{"default":0},"name":"Abilities","flags":{},"_id":"abilities","title":{"level":1,"show":true},"video":{}},{"image":{},"sort":200,"type":"text","src":null,"text":{"content":"\u003ch1\u003eGroup Suites\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNew \u0027group suites\u0027 of abilities are unlocked for purchase once all players reach a higher die type (i.e., one d6 from every player). Abilities from group suites cost 10 turbo tokens for an individual, or 18 for the entire group.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Criminal Conspiracy (d6):\u003c/strong\u003e Heists, cons, and criminal operations\n  \u003cul\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHot:\u003c/strong\u003e Roll Hot in response to the first attack of an encounter to dissuade an opponent.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eItem:\u003c/strong\u003e When in a new location, produce a single useful item.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTech:\u003c/strong\u003e Once per episode, add your Tech Die to a Sneak Die.\u003c/li\u003e\n  \u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e La Familia (d6):\u003c/strong\u003e Family bonds and mutual support\n  \u003cul\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSkill Die:\u003c/strong\u003e Lend a teammate a skill die.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTokens:\u003c/strong\u003e Spend tokens for other people at a 1:1 exchange rate.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTough:\u003c/strong\u003e Roll Tough on someone else\u0027s behalf.\u003c/li\u003e\n  \u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Diesel Circus (d8):\u003c/strong\u003e Vehicle-based mayhem and stunts\n  \u003cul\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDouble Explosion:\u003c/strong\u003e Doubles your amount of tokens.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDrive Check:\u003c/strong\u003e On a successful Drive Check, make another skill check.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eInjury Advantage:\u003c/strong\u003e Roll twice on the first roll after an injury.\u003c/li\u003e\n  \u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Tactical Command (d8):\u003c/strong\u003e Military precision and coordination\n  \u003cul\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReroll:\u003c/strong\u003e Reroll on a failure.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eShared Tokens:\u003c/strong\u003e Spend Turbo Tokens across scenes.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eToken Gain:\u003c/strong\u003e Characters gain a Turbo Token at the end of a scene where they have zero.\u003c/li\u003e\n  \u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Alpha Squad (d10):\u003c/strong\u003e Elite team operations\n  \u003cul\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGroup Explosion:\u003c/strong\u003e In a scene where everyone uses a different skill, reduce the range to Blow Up by 1.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSkill Add:\u003c/strong\u003e Two people roll the same skill and add the totals together.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSuit Up:\u003c/strong\u003e The group may \u0027suit up\u0027 and each take 2 Turbo Tokens.\u003c/li\u003e\n  \u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Marauders (d10):\u003c/strong\u003e Destructive force and chaos\n  \u003cul\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e+10:\u003c/strong\u003e Beating an opponent by more than 10 means you defeat an additional opponent.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDestroyer:\u003c/strong\u003e Gain a Turbo Token on any turn where you destroy an object.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFirestarter:\u003c/strong\u003e Start a fire, short circuit electronics, or dissolve a structure as part of any action.\u003c/li\u003e\n  \u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e The Continentals (d12):\u003c/strong\u003e Sophisticated espionage\n  \u003cul\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHot Checks:\u003c/strong\u003e Two successful Hot Checks auto-succeeds on stealing from an opponent.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMelee:\u003c/strong\u003e Lower the DC of a Weapons Checks using melee weapons.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWits:\u003c/strong\u003e Turbo Tokens for Wits help increase the die type.\u003c/li\u003e\n  \u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e The Ones (d12):\u003c/strong\u003e Peak performance and excellence\n  \u003cul\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMax Roll:\u003c/strong\u003e Treat a Nat 1 as a max die roll.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReroll:\u003c/strong\u003e Reroll a failure with a different skill.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTurbo Tokens:\u003c/strong\u003e Accept a Nat 1 to gain half the Turbo Tokens of the die value.\u003c/li\u003e\n  \u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e Bustin\u0027 Makes Me Feel Good (d20):\u003c/strong\u003e Supernatural encounters\n  \u003cul\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGM:\u003c/strong\u003e Become the GM for 60 seconds.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGroup Explosion:\u003c/strong\u003e Everybody else at the table graduates all of their lowest die type up by one.\u003c/li\u003e\n    \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTrack Restart:\u003c/strong\u003e Restart that skill track, now rolling a second die and taking the better result.\u003c/li\u003e\n  \u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003e Compendiums Available\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePlayer Abilities:\u003c/strong\u003e Individual character abilities\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGroup Abilities:\u003c/strong\u003e Team-based powers\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRules Reference:\u003c/strong\u003e Journal with quick rules and full PDF access\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFor complete rules, character creation, and advanced mechanics, see the full PDF rulebook linked above.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","format":1},"ownership":{"default":0},"name":"Group Suites","flags":{},"_id":"group-suites","title":{"level":1,"show":true},"video":{}}]}
